add('create-undead', '''KEEP Action, 60 feet, V/S/F, instantaneous creation and all four named alternatives: Ghoul, Ghast, Wight and Mummy. NEW choose exactly one of those four profiles and one distinct perceived Small or Medium Humanoid corpse within range/line of effect. The real corpse must not be summoned, copied, illusory, previously raised, already consumed or a severed fragment; it must retain a substantially continuous torso/head and a legal whole-body space. No arbitrary 24-hour age gate is added: actual decay, missing anatomy and remaining matter determine whether the required body exists. Do not repair harvested/destroyed organs, invent missing limbs or consume a living identity. A hidden ineligible body causes paid failure without a replacement selection. An independently legal resurrection completed before this conversion makes the body living and unavailable.

At resolution consume that physical corpse allocation once and create the chosen finite animation in its original real space. The four explicitly NEW complete profiles are printed immediately below and stored as structured records, rather than substituting a generic zombie. The current 67-record bestiary candidate contains no exact profile for these names; these are proposed spell-created profiles, not silently imported external monster statistics. All have mechanical type Undead, the corpse's actual Small/Medium size, physical mass and surviving anatomy, ordinary sight/hearing and darkvision 60, and no automatic type-derived resistances or immunities. Base HP/AC, six ability scores, permitted movement and Actions are separately supplied for each. Saving throws use original creator's current PB; other checks use its printed ability modifier without proficiency. Actual source-qualified maximum-HP modifiers apply. Attack criticals follow ordinary rules. Genuine usable worn armor may replace base AC under its own rules without creating a second formula or proficiency. Real carried/worn gear retains its prior damage, charges and actual inventory; equipping a new weapon does not silently add an unprinted attack profile.

NEW conversion itself is instantaneous and permanent: later dispelling/antimagic does not recreate the former corpse, undo physical damage or restore the former person. Creator command authority is a separate ongoing rank-six control relation until dispelled/released, with at most two active Create Undead control relations per creator across all four profiles. Before casting at full capacity, declare which existing relation a successfully created new body will release. Failed creation leaves that old relation intact. Creation never destroys a released body to make room. Newborn authority is part of this explicitly created animation chassis, not a hostile control attempt against a living target; it grants no control over a surviving original person. A later hostile control spell still needs its own actual hard-control admission.

While that authority operates, use the shared created-companion command, profile and original-owner statistics. NEW no voluntary movement, Dodge, command, attack or support during its creation numbered round; outside initiative its first potential opportunity is the next ordinary six-second cycle. Passive defenses and conditions still operate. No automatic Wizard standard-minion slot, Corpse Harvest, Auto-Raise, Ghoul Lash, elite identity, class repertoire or monster harvest recipe is gained. These two spell-control slots are separate from genuine other class slots, but all owned bodies retain the one shared command and offensive allowance. Healing can restore its legal current HP without repairing anatomy, curing Wounds, refreshing body provenance or creating resources.

This is an HP-only animated creature: at zero HP it is destroyed without a new dying/death-save/Wound track and leaves its same consumed physical remains and real surviving gear. Actual existing injuries and anatomy restrictions remain through creation and healing. Dispel of creator authority, voluntary release or an admitted slot replacement leaves the living animation with its real profile and present HP. Suppression releases only that relation's control while suppressed; it does not erase the permanent body. A released/suppressed animation has ordinary Director-controlled agency based on actual events, no guaranteed loyalty or automatic hostility, and only its finite profile/basic actions. It regains an independent regular opportunity under the no-duplicate-cycle transition, not an immediate free turn; a suppressed relation resumes with all spent budgets/history retained. Original creation source statistics remain the stated original-owner formulas even after release, not a free new owner's level. Caster incapacity/death alone ends neither body nor relation; unavailable phases give no invented commands. Actual rest may meet genuine needs but supplies no unprinted class/resource recovery. No repeated creator binding ritual is granted by recasting on the now-living animation. Its CR remains unrated: none of these new profiles qualifies for Command Undeath's exact CR 2 predicate without a separate actual CR decision.

Keep original corpse, conversion, animation, current controller, injuries, material loss and inventory events in one physical-provenance ledger. The original body is not simultaneously available for resurrection, harvesting or another animation. A genuine resurrection source must meet its own consumed-body reconstruction requirements; this spell supplies none and decides no soul ownership or destination. The four profiles' varied movement and attack roles, permanent released bodies, two-control cap and unrated CR are consequential new designs for actual GPT review.''', [
    'IN6-11-A: A legal corpse becomes one Ghast, not several generic zombies. Its base HP is 50 before actual qualified modifiers, its real missing hand remains missing, and its real armor is neither repaired nor duplicated. It cannot act in the creation numbered round. On a later lawful command it chooses its 15-foot exhalation instead of its melee attack, spending the same shared offensive allowance; the cone can affect allies.',
    'IN6-11-B: A creator already controlling a Ghoul and a Wight successfully creates a Mummy and releases the declared Ghoul relation. The Ghoul remains a real animation at its existing HP and gains no immediate bonus turn or refreshed corpse status. The Mummy uses base HP 70/AC 16 and its distinct strike, subject to real modifiers. Neither released Ghoul nor Mummy gains CR 2 merely because Command Undeath requires that rating.'
], 'NEW one eligible corpse/one distinct named profile, four complete source-transparent designs, permanent conversion separated from two-slot dispellable authority, release agency, no creation-round actions and no invented CR.')

add('circle-of-death', '''KEEP Action, 60 feet, V/S/M-or-F, instantaneous 8d6 necrotic and a 60-foot-radius sphere. NEW choose a perceived point within the casting range and caster line of effect. At resolution snapshot every actual creature whose occupied space intersects the 60-foot-radius sphere and has center-to-recipient line of effect under the existing area exposure rule, including allies and the caster when inside. The radius is not reduced to a diameter, a caster-centered 60-foot envelope or a six-target limit. The far edge can be 120 feet from a caster who places the center 60 feet away. An exposed part behind partial cover uses the actual saving-throw/cover rules; total obstruction from the center prevents exposure. No individual perception of each recipient is required.

NEW each recipient makes CON against the actual casting source's DC. Roll 8d6 necrotic once for the event, full on failure, half rounded down on success before that recipient's defenses. A successful save does not erase independently real immunity/resistance/vulnerability rules or grant a condition; those rules process the appropriate resulting packet. There is no separate initial attack, recurring damage, continuing area, entry pulse, concentration or target cap. Actual typed damage, temporary HP, damage sharing, floors, Instant Death, Wounds and dying/death responses use their already reviewed order. No automatic maximum-HP reduction, instant kill threshold, corpse destruction, resurrection block or extra death-save failure is supplied merely by the word Death.

Objects, nonanimated corpses, structures and illusions receive no creature-damage packet from this proposal. An actual Undead or Construct creature is not excluded by type alone; its genuine necrotic defenses control its result. An unseen living enemy in the exposed area can receive damage without giving the caster its identity, position or statistics through a new diagnostic channel. Ordinary witnessed sounds and consequences remain ordinary evidence. A transformed creature retains its one actual current HP/life identity; it does not receive separate damage to invented inner/outer bodies. Actual independently present carried creatures are separate area recipients, but carried objects are not.

Retain the existing ordinary material-or-focus alternative. No external black pearl, mandatory expensive reagent, blood sacrifice, consumed soul or harvesting benefit is imported. Actual class costs and source-specific surcharges remain real and are committed before Counterspell/hidden outcome; no refund for immune recipients or empty area. A real subsequent cast costs another Action/RP/cadence and creates one new damage event with its own snapshot; no shared-family periodic cap is invented for genuinely separate instantaneous casts. A copy/echo must satisfy its own actual source permissions and event lineage and does not obtain a free independent cast by reprocessing this record. After the packet resolves there is no persistent Circle of Death area to dispel, suppress or trigger again. Its only lasting consequences are the actual resolved injuries, HP changes and other genuinely triggered effects from those events.''', [
    'IN6-12-A: The caster places the center 60 feet away. The sphere has radius 60, so an exposed creature at the far boundary can be 120 feet from the caster. A shared roll of 29 necrotic becomes 14 on a successful CON save before resistance. The caster is included if its own occupied space is within the real sphere; allies are not selectively omitted.',
    'IN6-12-B: A creature behind total cover from the center receives no packet, while a currently unseen creature with area line of effect does. An Undead with necrotic immunity takes zero through that defense, not through a blanket type exclusion. The resulting corpse of a creature genuinely killed by damage is not additionally disintegrated or made unusable for resurrection solely by this spell\'s title.'
], 'NEW perceived sphere origin, all-creature snapshot and CON-half resolution preserving the full 60-foot radius and unpriced material/focus alternative.')

add('eyebite', '''KEEP Action, 60 feet, V/S/F and all three alternatives: asleep, panicked or sickened. Preserve Core Instantaneous as a metadata conflict. NEW declare one perceived creature with line of effect and one of the three modes before commitment/hidden outcomes. The creature makes initial WIS against the actual class DC; success establishes nothing. On failure attempt only the declared mode, concentration up to 60 elapsed seconds. No mode switch, free repeated gaze, additional target or later retargeting Action is granted. Another attempt requires a genuinely new paid spell, with normal concentration displacement and encounter histories.

ASLEEP: impose actual magically caused Unconscious, including its real inherited Incapacitated, awareness, movement, speech, held-item, Prone, saves and attack consequences subject to actual component immunities. This whole-Action effect claims the shared hard-control allowance once on establishment; an initially blocked application produces no alternative fear/sickness. Actual magical-sleep or Unconscious immunity applies within its stated scope. End this Eyebite sleep application when the target receives positive post-defense/pre-temp-HP damage, when another creature in physical reach spends an Action rousing this application's sleeper, on a successful ending save, or at the spell's ordinary end. If the helper cannot distinguish multiple Eyebite sleep sources, select one in neutral stable application order; this is not ordinary Sleep's separate all-Sleep wake rule. The waking attack resolves its actual hit/critical using the prior conditions before its damage wakes the target. Fully prevented zero damage does not wake; temp HP or a floor does not negate a real positive defended damage event. Awakening clears no unrelated Unconscious, zero-HP state or other source.

PANICKED: NEW actual Frightened toward the caster, plus a movement-only flight instruction while that relation is operative. At each future actual regular target START after normal processing, the creature must spend as much of its currently available ordinary movement as safely possible increasing distance from the caster's actual location known to that creature. With no actual known source location or no safe legal increasing-distance route, it makes no compelled movement and gains no secret locator. Use its real mode, terrain costs and remaining budget; actual controller chooses safe route details. It cannot be forced to Dash, spend an Action, expend RP/charges, leap into known serious danger, abandon valuable property or divulge secrets. Movement can provoke normal opportunity attacks; it is not push/pull. This soft mode claims no whole-Action guard. Fear immunity/suppression prevents or suspends the linked flight instruction as well as Frightened. Outside initiative use the existing shared six-second control cycle without replaying a passed START; an attached companion uses only a real existing phase and no fabricated off-screen cycle. Earliest actual instructions arbitrate shared movement.

SICKENED: NEW impose actual Poisoned, meaning disadvantage on attacks and ability checks under the current condition, without creating a toxin, consumable, infection, disease, new exhaustion track or automatic ongoing damage. Actual Poisoned immunity blocks it; disease-only or ordinary inhalation protection does not automatically block this magical condition source. No fear or whole-Action restriction is added, so no hard-control claim is made. Its real condition cure/removal rules apply. These definitions keep the source's three options distinct instead of silently treating Panicked/Sickened as nonexistent Core names.

Each established mode permits a WIS ending save at every actual regular END, including the upcoming END of a current turn, using the shared END-only/specific companion bridge. The Asleep save is expressly allowed without an Action or conscious self-rousing; its WIS is not a STR/DEX automatic failure. A successful save ends only that application. Damage does not independently end Panicked or Sickened. One active Eyebite per caster/recipient; genuinely established later same-caster Eyebite replaces that caster's older one, while different casters' modes retain independent saves, concentration and actual compatible condition effects. Any applicable stronger prevention still retains its scope. Suppression suspends the affected mode while clock/saves and used movement/control histories persist; no missed flight or drop-held-item event is replayed on return. Target death, concentration end, actual removal or original expiry ends the remaining source. No mode heals, stabilizes, resets resources, gives the caster private thoughts or changes actual faction standing.''', [
    'IN6-13-A: Asleep is declared, the target fails WIS and the shared hard-control allowance is available. It becomes actually Unconscious and later receives 8 positive defended damage fully absorbed by temporary HP. That damage still wakes this Eyebite sleep after the waking attack\'s hit/critical is resolved. Its separate zero-HP Unconscious source, if present, would remain, and hard-control history stays spent.',
    'IN6-13-B: A Panicked target with Speed 30 can safely retreat only 10 feet before a known lethal drop, so it spends only those 10 feet rather than being forced to Dash or jump. It still has its ordinary Action. A separately Sickened target suffers Poisoned attack/check disadvantage, not flight or sleep, and can end its own application on its actual WIS ending save. Neither case creates a free repeated gaze next turn.'
], 'NEW one-target predeclared mode, WIS/concentration minute, exact sleep/wake, Frightened-safe-flight and Poisoned interfaces, and no imported repeated gaze.')

